WE ARE SPECIALISTS WHO ARE ABLE TO QUICKLY AND EASILY FIND AND CONSUME APIS, CREATE NEW, SETUP INTEGRATIONS ACROSS THE ENTERPRISE AND MAKE BUSINESSES FASTER AND MORE PRODUCTIVE AS A WHOLE.

SynergySoft was established in Geneva, Switzerland, to bring to customers its 10+ years of the API-led approach practical application and deep knowledge of MuleSoft Anypoint Platform.

We provide integration of full-cycle API Governance solutions that fits API Management, API Integration, Policy Management, Life Cycle Management, Metadata Management, and Data Quality tracking operational analytics. API Governance can be deployed On-Premises, in Cloud, and as Hybrid one.

SynergySoft has a successful track record with US and EU customers which represent the following industries: Automotive, Banking, Insurance, Manufacturing, Retail, Telecom and others.
HAVING THE RIGHT API MANAGEMENT TOOL IS CRUCIAL FOR MANAGING API COMPLEXITY
Successful organisations think about these APIs as products.  That’s where SynergySoft gets in and offers API-led integration solutions.

SynergySoft provides integration of full-cycle API Governance solutions that fits API Management, API Integration, Policy Management, Life Cycle Management Metadata Management, and Data Quality tracking operational analytics.

We assist clients in the management of the full life cycle of API:
- The planning, design, implementation, testing, publication, operation, consumption, maintenance, versioning and retirement of APIs;
- Delivery of a developer portal through which to target, market to and govern communities of developers who embed APIs;
-Runtime management;
- Estimation of APIs’ value;
- The use of analytics to understand patterns of API usage.

linkedinJobDescription:
After completing my final year of undergraduate studies, I decided to take a gap year to volunteer under the French Civic Service program with the organization Unis-Cité Marseille. With this program I had the opportunity to work within the association ENJOY CLUB, which promote a game based learning approach based on the theory of multiple intelligences to help high school students to develop their abilities.

Throughout my time as a volunteer, my main objective was to promote the various workshops offered by the association to its target audience of teenagers and schoolchildren. To accomplish this task, I had to carry out a number of different missions, such as :

-Contributing to the development and implementation of communication strategies to promote the association's ludo pedagogy workshops involving information monitoring to identify key partners, associations and public schools;
- Producing engaging visual and written content for social media platforms (flyers, banner, presentations templates, infographic, teaser ) using digital tools such as Canva, Adobe, CapCut and Illustrator;
-Contributing to the development of workshops tailored to various audiences, ensuring effective room setups, distributing both digital and printed materials, and providing hands-on support to guide and assist young participants throughout the sessions.

These months of volunteering have been incredibly rewarding for me on both a personal and professional level. it gave me a profound awareness of the multitude of challenges our societies face. From promoting education for all, fostering solidarity and promoting equality, this experience highlighted the vital role each of us can play in shaping a more inclusive and equitable world.

For my first internship as a Master’s Degree Student, I opted to be a Marketing Project Assistant for ENJOY CLUB. Around this time, the association became quite successful among many different institutions of the city of Marseille, and even outside of the city. Therefore, the association’s purpose evolved, and thus, needed to develop a new strategy in order to have an added-value. 

My primary mission, along with all related tasks, was to define a new scaleable marketing strategy for ENJOY CLUB, revamp its branding and identity, which would successfully contribute to the launch of its new innovative offerings by September 2024 for the new school year, strengthen its visibility, and confirm its expertise. To achieve that, I proposed some strategic recommandations, which turned into additional tasks :

- Redefined and segmented the target audience to define the field of action;
- Refined the educational content of the new workshops and their formats (collective and individual workshops), to ensure that the target audience understands their relevance, and sees how they can respond to their needs;
- Identified the association’s positioning (its « personality »), which we concluded  was « Supporting young people in key areas of their development through play-based learning and Multiple Intelligences »,  to create a unique differentiator;
- Clarified the association’s mission, known as its "purpose" in the non-profit sector, so the target audience can understand the authentic impact the association aims to deliver at them.
- Defined the association’s new values in line with its updated mission, and build an organizational culture that allows individuals to identify with it.

linkedinPreviousJobDescription:
During my gap year, I had the opportunity to be a volunteer under the French Civic Service program within ENJOY CLUB, an association whose purpose is to help young people (middle schoolers, high schoolers and young adults) to discover their full potential, and for them to be aware of their unique value. To achieve that, they propose unique and innovative workshops, based on the Multiple Intelligences' theory, combined with a playful educational approach and game-based learning tools.

Throughout my entire Civic Service, my main task was to promote the organization’s workshops towards its target audience. In order to succeed in doing this task, I had to accomplish several complementary tasks :

- Determined the target’s needs and expectations by analyzing their behavior during workshop sessions, in order to constantly improve them;
- Developed questionnaires to gather participants’ impressions, in addition to conducting workshop assessments to evaluate if the marketing objectives were achieved or not;
- Wrote and shared educational workshop descriptions to institutions where we were scheduled to conduct workshop sessions; 
- Observed workshop sessions to identify strengths, as well as areas of improvement (positive and negative points) for the association to address;
- Created content (photos and videos) showcasing each workshops.

During these nine enriching months of Civic Service, we collaborated with the following institutions :

- Les Déterminés;
- Eloquentia;
- Trace Talent;
- Campus Co;
- Impact Jeunes;
- Ludorium-CFA;
- Saint-Joseph Middle School;
- Chioni Maoulana Charif Association (CMC).

linkedinCompanyDescription:
Créé en 1982, le CIDFF du Var adhère à la FNCIDFF et est membre du réseau des 104 CIDFF. Le CIDFF est un acteur majeur de la politique publique d'information des femmes sur le département du Var, il exerce une mission d'intérêt général, confiée par l'État, dont l'objectif est de favoriser l'autonomie sociale, professionnelle et personnelle des femmes et de promouvoir l'égalité entre les femmes et les hommes.
Le CIDFF/VAR informe, oriente et accompagne le public dans les domaines :
- de l'accès au droit ;
- de la lutte contre les violences sexistes ;
- du soutien à la parentalité ;
- de l'emploi, de la formation professionnelle et de la création d'entreprise ;
- de l'éducation et de la citoyenneté.

